.TH UPDATE-NOTIFY-DNS 1 "August 2026" "mu2edaq-notify 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
update\-notify\-dns.sh \- inspect or repair the proxy's public A record from the operator's host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/update\-notify\-dns.sh
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-\-instance\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIZONE_ID\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIRECORD\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the proxy instance's state, the public IPv4 the EC2 API reports for it,
the value of the
.B A
record in Route 53, and what DNS actually answers \(en then, unless
.B \-\-check
was given, upserts the record to the API address.
.PP
This is the break\-glass path. In normal operation the instance publishes its
own record at boot; see
.BR mu2edaq-notify-dns-update (1).
Use this when the instance cannot: before the instance profile is attached
(the first cutover away from the Elastic IP, or a rebuilt instance), or when
the instance\-side updater has failed and left the record stale.
.PP
The address always comes from the EC2 API, not from a stored value, unless
.B \-\-ip
overrides it. Nothing is written when the record is already correct.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Report only, change nothing. Exits 1 if the record is stale, which makes it
usable as a monitoring probe.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ip " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Publish this address instead of asking the API.
.TP
.B \-\-instance \fIID\fR
EC2 instance to read the address from. Default
.BR i\-000ee813ecd9a47b3 .
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone " " \fIZONE_ID\fR
Hosted zone. Default
.BR Z2OL4WKH228GKD .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-record " " \fIRECORD\fR
Record name. Default
.BR notify.andrewnorman.org .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
Record TTL. Default 60.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-wait
Do not poll the change to
.BR INSYNC .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the change batch, submit nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_INSTANCE_ID,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_REGION,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_DNS_NAME,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ROUTE53_ZONE_ID,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_TTL.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Record correct, or updated.
.TP
.B 1
Stale under
.BR \-\-check ,
or the update could not be made.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check whether DNS agrees with the running instance:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/update\-notify\-dns.sh \-\-check
.fi
.RE
.PP
Repair a stale record after the instance\-side updater failed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/update\-notify\-dns.sh
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-notify-dns-update (1),
.BR install-notify-dns-updater.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-caa.sh (1)
